[
  {
    "text": "NETWORK SECURITY / NONZERO-SUM DIFFERENTIAL GAMES",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 68,
    "width": 818.9912109375,
    "size": 27
  },
  {
    "text": "A Resource-Constrained Network Defense",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 135,
    "width": 1750.1103515625002,
    "size": 87
  },
  {
    "text": "Decision Method Based on a Nonzero-Sum",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 232,
    "width": 1774.0268554687502,
    "size": 87
  },
  {
    "text": "Differential Game",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 329,
    "width": 720.3837890625001,
    "size": 87
  },
  {
    "text": "[Author names in manuscript order]",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 446,
    "width": 579.958984375,
    "size": 34
  },
  {
    "text": "[Department, University / Organization, City, Country]     [Corresponding email]",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 497,
    "width": 972.603515625,
    "size": 28
  },
  {
    "text": "Scheduling isolation and recovery reduces cumulative loss",
    "x": 116,
    "y": 620,
    "width": 1211.55859375,
    "size": 43
  },
  {
    "text": "Main capacity B = 1.2. The attack plan is computed jointly with dynamic defense and then fixed for all comparisons.",
    "x": 116,
    "y": 680,
    "width": 1577.5185546875,
    "size": 31
  },
  {
    "text": "01",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 842,
    "width": 34.4814453125,
    "size": 31
  },
  {
    "text": "Model and decision problem",
    "x": 150,
    "y": 840,
    "width": 553.56005859375,
    "size": 41
  },
  {
    "text": "Choose source isolation and local recovery for each asset and time interval",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 929,
    "width": 1030.43212890625,
    "size": 31
  },
  {
    "text": "while attacks propagate across a directed network.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 973,
    "width": 696.1376953125,
    "size": 31
  },
  {
    "text": "Six logical assets. Direct attacks enter at the API gateway and Web application.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 1570,
    "width": 1018.73828125,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "Recovery lowers local compromise; isolation suppresses outgoing propagation.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 1611,
    "width": 1015.52392578125,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "02",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 1778,
    "width": 34.4814453125,
    "size": 31
  },
  {
    "text": "Compute a defense schedule",
    "x": 150,
    "y": 1776,
    "width": 567.3134765625,
    "size": 41
  },
  {
    "text": "ABR-DAD: Alternating Best Response for Dynamic Defense Action",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 1864,
    "width": 950.1416015625,
    "size": 30
  },
  {
    "text": "Decision.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 1906,
    "width": 133.3740234375,
    "size": 30
  },
  {
    "text": "1 Parameterize controls over six time intervals.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 1972,
    "width": 601.1552734375,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "2 Fix the attack plan and optimize defense locally.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 2026,
    "width": 639.96826171875,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "3 Fix defense and optimize the attack locally.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 2080,
    "width": 577.0830078125,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "4 Repeat, then check unilateral deviations and feasibility.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 2134,
    "width": 730.28173828125,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "RK4 evaluates state trajectories; SLSQP computes local numerical responses",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 2215,
    "width": 999.3671875,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "under control bounds and instantaneous capacity constraints.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 2256,
    "width": 788.33837890625,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "03",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 2393,
    "width": 34.4814453125,
    "size": 31
  },
  {
    "text": "Allocate resources across assets and time",
    "x": 150,
    "y": 2391,
    "width": 829.529296875,
    "size": 41
  },
  {
    "text": "At B = 1.2, capacity binds in intervals 2–4. All three capacities show reduced effort",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 2935,
    "width": 1053.4306640625,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "in the final interval.",
    "x": 85,
    "y": 2976,
    "width": 241.798828125,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "04",
    "x": 1230.9685039370079,
    "y": 842,
    "width": 34.4814453125,
    "size": 31
  },
  {
    "text": "Compare cumulative defense losses",
    "x": 1295.9685039370079,
    "y": 840,
    "width": 708.67138671875,
    "size": 41
  },
  {
    "text": "2.41%",
    "x": 1230.9685039370079,
    "y": 933,
    "width": 283.544921875,
    "size": 100
  },
  {
    "text": "14.79%",
    "x": 1775.6324409448819,
    "y": 933,
    "width": 339.16015625,
    "size": 100
  },
  {
    "text": "Lower total loss than fixed-mean",
    "x": 1230.9685039370079,
    "y": 1049,
    "width": 417.498046875,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "defense",
    "x": 1230.9685039370079,
    "y": 1088,
    "width": 103.19921875,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "Lower total loss than no defense",
    "x": 1775.6324409448819,
    "y": 1049,
    "width": 417.5546875,
    "size": 29
  },
  {
    "text": "The dynamic and fixed-mean plans have equal cumulative isolation and",
    "x": 1230.9685039370079,
    "y": 1175,
    "width": 950.56640625,
    "size": 30
  },
  {
    "text": "recovery inputs for each asset. Their timing differs.",
    "x": 1230.9685039370079,
    "y": 1218,
    "width": 671.9384765625,
    "size": 30
  },
  {
    "text": "Compromised fractions under the shared attack plan. Dynamic defense protects the",
    "x": 1230.9685039370079,
    "y": 2010,
    "width": 1036.533203125,
    "size": 28
  },
  {
    "text": "core database more strongly; some late-horizon state curves cross.",
    "x": 1230.9685039370079,
    "y": 2049,
    "width": 834.1484375,
    "size": 28
  },
  {
    "text": "Defense plan",
    "x": 1238.9685039370079,
    "y": 2187,
    "width": 168.05126953125,
    "size": 27
  },
  {
    "text": "Security loss",
    "x": 1593.9685039370079,
    "y": 2187,
    "width": 168.07763671875,
    "size": 27
  },
  {
    "text": "Total loss",
    "x": 1841.9685039370079,
    "y": 2187,
    "width": 126.02197265625,
    "size": 27
  },
  {
    "text": "Final state",
    "x": 2089.968503937008,
    "y": 2187,
    "width": 133.53662109375,
    "size": 27
  },
  {
